[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605250645-yakushi-wave-1c-r1.5-benzonatate-pmda-approval", :adr/title "yakushi Wave 1c R1.5 — Benzonatate PMDA approval contingency (conditional activation)", :adr/status "deferred", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# yakushi Wave 1c R1.5 — Benzonatate PMDA approval contingency\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-25 (template; conditional execution upon PMDA decision)\n**Status:** Deferred — **ISSUE THIS ADR ONLY IF PMDA approves benzonatate OTC by 2026-06-30**\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2605250630 (Wave 1c R1) established a PMDA jurisdiction monitoring window until 2026-06-30. Japan currently has benzonatate as Rx-only (Besibun formulation), with an OTC application under PMDA review since ~2023.\n\n**This ADR is a conditional placeholder:**\n- **If PMDA approves OTC before 2026-06-30:** This ADR is authored, approved by Council Lv6+, and merged immediately\n- **If PMDA does NOT approve by 2026-06-30:** This ADR is archived as \"deferred — no decision\" and benzonatate manufacturing remains blocked until a future Wave 2 or Wave 3 ADR\n\n## Decision\n\n(To be filled upon PMDA approval announcement.)\n\n### Template section (fill only upon PMDA OTC approval):\n\nBenzonatate OTC approval in Japan (PMDA decision date: [fill date]) unlocks `pharma_liquid_formulation` cell for benzonatate suspension manufacturing at R1.5 phase.\n\n**Manufacturing scope (unchanged from Wave 1c R0):**\n- Benzonatate 100–150 mg/5 mL suspension (non-sterile fill, amber BFS bottles)\n- Excipients: glycerin (suspending vehicle), xanthan gum (thickener), sodium benzoate 0.1% (preservative), colorant, flavor, purified water\n- Viscosity: 100–150 milli-centipoise @ 25°C\n- Particle size: ≤5 µm median (laser diffraction)\n- Microbial limits: USP <61>/<62> (TAMC ≤10⁴ CFU/mL, fungi ≤10² CFU/mL, *E. coli*/*S. aureus*/*P. aeruginosa* absent)\n- Resuspendability: <5 min hand-shake after 4-week settle test\n\n**Gate unlock condition:**\n- `COUNCIL_ATTESTATION_TX_HASH` + `SILEN_PHARMA_BASELINE_REVIEW_CID` (set during R1) must remain non-None\n- Additional `BENZONATATE_PMDA_OTC_APPROVAL_CID` gate marker: set to IPFS CID of official PMDA approval announcement record or Council-attested summary\n\n**Timeline (upon PMDA approval):**\n- T+0: PMDA approval announced (public news + official PMDA journal)\n- T+1: yakushi QA lead notifies Council Lv6+ + escalates to etzhayyim members\n- T+2-5: This ADR authored + Council ballot (≥3 affirmative within 5 days)\n- T+6-7: Merge to `feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1.5-benzonatate` branch + CI validation\n- T+8: Merge to main; `pharma_liquid_formulation` cell gate unlock\n- T+9+: Benzonatate suspension manufacturing operational at josephNode (Murakumo placement unchanged)\n\n## Consequences\n\nNone until PMDA decision arrives. Upon approval:\n\n1. **Operationalization:** `pharma_liquid_formulation` cell transitions from guaifenesin-only to guaifenesin + benzonatate dual-route\n2. **QC doubling:** Benzonatate suspension requires additional particle-size + resuspendability QC vs guaifenesin syrup (non-sterile fill complexity)\n3. **API coverage:** yakushi API catalog expands to include benzonatate as 20th API (Wave 1: 3, Wave 1b: 9, Wave 1c base: 7, Wave 1c benzonatate: +1)\n4. **No constitutional gate amendment:** 14 gates G1..G14 + 10 non-goals N1..N10 remain unchanged\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### 1. Skip benzonatate entirely if PMDA denies\n**Chosen.** R1.5 ADR is NOT issued; benzonatate manufacturing remains blocked; future Wave 2 or Wave 3 charter would be required.\n\n### 2. Preemptively unlock benzonatate in R1 pending PMDA decision\n**Rejected.** Would violate G1 (OTC-only perpetually off-patent in all-3 jurisdictions) until formal PMDA approval. Precautionary principle: no manufacturing until jurisdiction cleared.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605250630: yakushi Wave 1c R1 — baseline charter with benzonatate monitoring assignment\n- PMDA Japanese Pharmacopoeia OTC Status Review (benzonatate application timeline ~2023–2025)\n- Tessalon (benzonatate) USA OTC status (Parexel historical approval, reference for international recognition)\n- EMA decentralized procedure benzonatate approval (reference for non-JP jurisdiction precedent)\n\n---\n\n**Status:** DEFERRED — Will be issued only upon PMDA OTC approval announcement for benzonatate (expected decision window 2024–2025, monitoring deadline 2026-06-30).\n**Trigger:** PMDA official decision announcement via PMDA journal or equivalent public notice.\n**Owner:** yakushi QA lead (monitoring responsibility per ADR-2605250630).\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605250645-yakushi-wave-1c-r1.5-benzonatate-pmda-approval.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "yakushi/pharmaceutical/benzonatate-contingency", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z", :adr/date "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z", :adr/authoritative true}]
